# Festag elevated surfaces

Content should feel calm, precious, and lifted — never technical chrome.

## Floating plate (portal main)

Canonical tokens (`lib/design-tokens/elevated.ts` → `app/globals.css`):

```css
--festag-plate-radius: 12px;
--festag-plate-inset: 4px;           /* top / right / bottom */
--festag-plate-bg: #FFFFFF;          /* dark → #0D0D10 */
--festag-plate-border: rgba(15,23,42,0.055);
--festag-plate-shadow: /* soft inset light + contact + ambient */;
```

Utility: `.festag-elevated-plate`

Recipe for the Client Portal main column:

```css
.portal-app-main-col { padding: var(--festag-plate-inset) var(--festag-plate-inset) var(--festag-plate-inset) 0; }
.portal-app-main {
  background: var(--festag-plate-bg);
  border: 1px solid var(--festag-plate-border);
  border-radius: var(--festag-plate-radius);
  box-shadow: var(--festag-plate-shadow);
}
```

`--festag-content-panel` aliases the plate fill/border so settings and cards stay in the same family.

## Nested glass (light tiles inside the plate)

```css
--festag-glass-bg / -strong / -soft
--festag-glass-border / -edge
--festag-glass-blur
--festag-glass-shadow-soft
```

Utility: `.festag-glass` — use for nested tiles, not for the main floating plate.

## When to use

- **Plate:** `.portal-app-main`, large shells, settings workspace frames
- **Glass:** horizontal tiles, capsules, nested cards on the canvas/plate
- **Do not:** hard drop-shadows, thick borders, 20px+ radius on the main plate, full-bleed dark main without the floating plate on desktop

## Dark mode

Plate stays elevated on OLED canvas (`#000`): graphite fill, whisper hairline, soft ambient depth — no frosted blur.
